# What kind of auth participant this service is.
#
# Read by the pipeline-catalog auth-conformance gate, which CROSS-CHECKS this
# declaration against what the code actually does and fails on a contradiction
# (`authconformance --explain` prints the full standard).
#
# It is declared rather than inferred because inference guesses — a derived
# heuristic once reported this platform's own SPA client as a stranger holding
# internal audiences — and it is cross-checked because a declaration drifts the
# moment someone adds an outbound call.
#
# The correct auth env set and chart shape are a function of this type. There is
# no single standard set: an inbound-only service given CLIENT_ID/CLIENT_SECRET
# looks like it holds an identity it never spends.
type: inbound-resource-server
